    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter the slate with a heavy emphasis on speed and top-of-the-order efficiency, anchored by our two strongest plays: **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (80.92) and **Trea Turner** (79.76). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our top-rated hitter today against Warren, as his combination of leadoff duties and a strong platoon advantage against the right-hander makes him a critical engine for SB and R production. Similarly, **Trea Turner** benefits from a massive park factor boost and high-leverage leadoff placement, making him an elite start despite a moderate challenge from Young. **Junior Caminero** (76.86) also presents a high-ceiling profile, as he occupies the #3 hole and faces the highly hittable Fedde, leveraging an impressive xwOBA of 0.370. **Christian Yelich** rounds out our top-tier tier (74.33), benefiting significantly from a dynamic platoon advantage against Ryan Johnson, despite the minor defensive risk posed by the opposing catcher\u2019s pop time.\n\nOur lineup construction favors high-efficiency opportunities over raw talent, which forced a tough call regarding the bench. **Chase Meidroth** was the final cut, falling just short at 49.27; while his SP matchup against Martinez (4.84 xERA) looked appealing, his low-leverage #8 spot in the order diluted his efficiency, causing him to land below the thresholds set by our starters. We are monitoring **Dillon Dingler**, **Gary Sanchez**, **Colt Keith**, **Caleb Durbin**, and **Christian Yelich** closely as their lineups remain pending. **Colt Keith** carries the most risk today, as his platoon disadvantage against the lefty Springs dampens his outlook, though his high base projection keeps him firmly in the lineup. As a final reminder, **Hyeseong Kim** remains unavailable due to his status with the Oklahoma City Comets. Be advised that **Yordan Alvarez** faces a difficult test against Eovaldi, but his elite 0.477 xwOBA makes him an indispensable start regardless of the SP talent.",
